# =====================================================================
# Byte preservation for a frozen research record. Do not narrow or remove.
#
# This repository is the closed record of an experimental programme. File
# hashes are recorded as provenance inside the analysis manifests
# (prompt_hashes, frozen_hashes, frozen_baseline_file_hashes,
# distinct_file_hashes). A checkout must therefore be byte-identical to what
# was committed, on every machine, or those recorded hashes stop verifying.
#
# The experiment artifacts intentionally contain MIXED line endings, and the
# mix runs *within* a single file class rather than between classes — e.g. of
# 476 raw run records 466 contain CRLF and 4 are LF-only; of 27 execution
# plans and manifests 12 contain CRLF and 15 are LF-only. That is a property
# of how the records were written during execution, and it is part of the
# frozen bytes. No convention-setting rule can preserve both sides of such a
# mix: any EOL normalization would rewrite one side of it. So conversion is
# disabled outright rather than standardized.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion only. It does NOT mark files binary:
# git diff, blame and merge remain fully text-aware. Attributes take
# precedence over core.autocrlf, so this holds regardless of the cloning
# machine's git configuration.
# =====================================================================
* -text
